   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "print(np.unique(biogrid[\"Organism ID Interactor A\"]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17530a8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What do those IDs mean?\n",
    "\n",
    "Biogrids \"Organism Interactor IDs\" show us which organism a protein belongs to. Since we want to work with human cancer, we simply select only rows with a human ID (9606)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "38ae1a89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Filtering non-human proteins\n",
    "biogrid = biogrid[(biogrid['Organism ID Interactor A'] == 9606) & (biogrid['Organism ID Interactor B'] == 9606)]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "954d6875",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "913180\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# let's see how much data we have left\n",
    "print(len(biogrid))"
   ]
  },
